urance and cannot guarantee the safety, accuracy of information, or quality of venues, third-party services, or other attendees.*\n* *By attending, you release TILE, its organizers, and affiliates from any and all claims or liability, and you agree to conduct yourself respectfully and in accordance with local laws and venue rules.*\n* ***If you do not agree with this disclaimer, please do not attend TILE events.***","startDate":"2026-10-03T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Madison Avenue Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"14 Madison Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto's BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event + Class","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tilesocial/"},"performer":"Toronto's BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event + Class"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Fast Friends Toronto: Meet New People | Play 50+ Board Games | 25–45","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/events/316495331/","description":"Want to expand your social circle in Toronto but find it difficult to turn a room full of strangers into actual conversations?\n\n*Fast Friends makes that first step easy.*\nJoin us for a professionally hosted social evening where you’ll meet 20+ people through relaxed, guided conversations and rotations — with fun themed rounds to help you discover common interests and get beyond the usual small talk.\nAnd when the hosted rounds finish, the evening keeps going. 🎲\n\nAt Stout Irish Pub, you’ll have access to 50+ board games, making it easy to stay, grab a drink, join a game and continue chatting with the people you’ve just met.\n\nBook Early & Save: [https://toronto3rdoct.eventbrite.co.uk](https://toronto3rdoct.eventbrite.co.uk)\nEarly Bird: CAD $10 \\| Regular: CAD $15 \\| Door: CAD $20 cash\nAdvance tickets help us plan the right space and group size and ensure a well-organised experience for everyone.\n\n🤝 What to Expect\n7:00 PM — Welcome & Drinks\nMeet your host, Kruttika, grab a drink and settle in.\nComing alone? You're in good company. Many of our guests arrive solo, and our host will help you get comfortable, make introductions and get the evening started.\n\n7:30–8:30 PM — Hosted Fast Friends\nThis is where the magic happens.\nYou'll have a series of short, guided conversations, moving around the group so you get the chance to meet a variety of people rather than spending the whole evening talking to just one person.\nNo need to walk up to strangers and figure out what to say — we've created the structure for you.\n\n✨ Themed Connection Rounds\nAlongside the regular Fast Friends conversations, we'll introduce interactive themed rounds with fun prompts and challenges designed to uncover shared interests, experiences and unexpected connections.\nThey're simple, social and designed to get the conversation flowing naturally.\n\n🎲 8:30 PM onwards — 50+ Board Games & Socialising\nDon't feel like heading home after the hosted rounds?\nStay and keep the evening going at Stout.\n\nWith 50+ board games available, you can join a game with people you've met, grab another drink, continue a conversation or simply mingle and see where the evening takes you.\nYou don't need to be a serious gamer — the games are simply another easy way to keep people interacting.\n\n❤️ Why This Event?\n✔️ Meet 20+ new people in one evening\n✔️ Professionally hosted conversations and rotations\n✔️ Fun themed connection rounds\n✔️ 50+ board games at Stout 🎲\n✔️ Reserved area for our group\n✔️ Easy-to-reach Toronto location\n✔️ A relaxed pub atmosphere\n✔️ Most guests attend solo\n✔️ Meet members from across our Toronto social communities\n✔️ Ages 25–45\n✔️ Friendship-focused — not a dating event\n\n👥 Who Should Come?\nWhether you've recently moved to Toronto, have lived here for years, work from home and want a bigger social circle, or simply feel like meeting some different people — you're welcome.\nYou don't need to know anyone beforehand.\nCome by yourself, bring a friend, or come somewhere in between. The evening is designed to make it easy to get involved.\n\n💳 Why Book in Advance?\nYour ticket helps us plan the right space, manage the group size and create a comfortable experience for everyone.\nOnline tickets are also cheaper than paying at the door.\n\n🌍 About Fast Friends\nFor over 10 years, Fast Friends has been helping people make genuine connections through professionally hosted social events in 30+ cities around the world.\nOur goal is simple: make meeting new people easier, more relaxed and more enjoyable.\nCome solo. We'll guide the experience. You make the connections. ❤️","startDate":"2026-10-03T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Stout Irish pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"221 Carlton St., Toronto, ON M5A 2L2, Canada,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Singles in the city (13000+)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/"},"performer":"Toronto Singles in the city (13000+)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto First-Timers Welcome Local Speed Dating","url":"https://www.meetup.com/clay-buddies-pottery-and-social-club/events/316524966/","description":"**UPDATE: This event has been rescheduled and is now set to begin at 5:00 PM on Sun, Oct 4 (local time).**\n\nVirtual speed dating hosted over Zoom for Toronto residents who are single. Experience brief individual sessions paired by age group, all within the comfort of your own home.\n\nSimply confirm your attendance and we will contact you with the complete information. Availability is restricted and the gathering might be called off if participation levels are insufficient.","startDate":"2026-10-03T04:18:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"JM35+VH Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"JM35+VH Toronto, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Clay Buddies Pottery And Social Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/clay-buddies-pottery-and-social-club/"},"performer":"Clay Buddies Pottery And Social Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Cozy Cocktails Social and Paint Night - National Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/national-social-networking-group-toronto-20s-30s/events/316269240/","description":"A friendship social — not a dating event. Most guests come solo.\n✨ **[Get My Ticket →](https://nationalsocialnetworking.com/tickets?city=toronto)**\n[https://nationalsocialnetworking.com/tickets?city=toronto](https://nationalsocialnetworking.com/tickets?city=toronto)\n\nOur hosts run the room. They'll introduce you and fold you into a group — no standing on the edge with a drink.\n\n💬 Hosted mingling\n🎭 Come alone — most people do\n👕 Smart casual\n🍹 Please order one item from the venue\n\n📅 **[All Toronto Events](https://nationalsocialnetworking.com/tickets?city=toronto)**\n\n*Gratuity may be added automatically by some venues.*","startDate":"2026-10-03T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Celtic Irish Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto, ON","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1954 Yonge St unit# 1, Toronto, ON, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"National Social Networking Group - Toronto (20s-30s)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/national-social-networking-group-toronto-20s-30s/"},"performer":"National Social Networking Group - Toronto (20s-30s)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🇨🇦Japanese and English Language Exchange  (Page for everyone)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tjex-ca/events/316545497/","description":"～English description below～\n\nイベント参加費として、日本人の方(日本で生まれ育ち、現在英語を勉強している方)は2、日本人以外の方(日本語を勉強している方)は5頂いております。\n\n皆さんから頂いたお金は、こちらのサイトの維持費や将来のランゲージエクスチェンジ施設利用料やソーシャルイベント等のために使われます。ご理解の程、よろしくお願いいたします。\n\n予約受付開始：土曜日5:00PM\n\n予約取消締切：土曜日14:00PM(当日)\n\n予約受付締切：土曜日15:00PM(当日)\n\nスケジュール\n\n5.15 PM - 5:30PM - チェックイン、グループ分け\n\n5:30 PM - 6:15PM - 日本語の時間［または英語の時間］\n\n6:15PM - 7:00 PM - 英語の時間［または日本語の時間］\n\n【イベント内容】\n\nLanguage Exchangeへようこそ！このグループでは、皆さんのレベルに応じて、3〜4名のグループにわかれ、同じ席になった人たちで各45分間、それぞれ英語と日本語でフリートークを行なっていただきます。決まったディスカッショントピックなどはございませんので、気軽に質問をしながらそれぞれのセッションを楽しんでいただければと思います。\n\n開催場所：Atrium フードコート\n\nTJEXのサインボードを持ったオーガナイザーにお声がけください。(もしサインがなかったり、わからなければメッセージをお願いします！)\n\n予約規約（⚠️重要）\n\n・当日の不参加、もしくは15分以上の遅刻、また予約取消締切後の変更は原則不参加(No-Show)とみなします。不参加(No-show)が3回になりますと会員登録が抹消され、退会となりますのでご注意ください。\n\n・イベントに遅れそうな場合は必ずオーガナイザーまでメッセージをお願いします。イベント開始時間にいるメンバーでグループを組み直すこともあるので、連絡なしで到着された場合はイベントに参加できない可能性もあります。原則、30分以上遅れての参加はご遠慮いただいております。あらかじめご了承ください。\n\nキャンセル待ち\n\n・満席の場合、”キャンセル待ち”リスト(waiting-list)にご登録いただくことが可能です。“参加予定”リスト（going-list)中に空席が発生した場合は、”キャンセル待ち”への登録が早かった方を優先に、オーガナイザーが”参加予定”へ移動しますので、当日の参加状況の変更がないかご自身でご確認ください。\n\n※ご注意※\n\n・空席ができた際は、自動的に”キャンセル待ち”より”参加予定”へ変更されます。この時にMeetupよりお知らせがあるかはわかりません。\n\n・システムにより自動的に”参加予定”とされ、それに気づかずに参加しなかった場合でも、不参加とみなされますのでご了承ください。\n\nInstagramアカウント @tjex.ca\n\n最新情報やミートアップの様子を掲載しています。\n\nぜひこちらもフォローお願いします！\n\n***Although our group is a non-profit organization, we collect $ 5 per English Speaker for every event. All the proceeds are used to run this website and for social events***\n\n*Canadian English speakers must be Native or Fluent in English in order to participate*\n\nRSVP:\nRSVP open: 5:00 PM\n\nRSVP cancel deadline: Saturday, 2:00 PM (day of the event)\n\nRSVP close: Saturday, 3:00 PM (day of the event)\n\nDay of Event:\n5:15 PM - 5:30 PM - Check-in and Group placement\n\n5:30 PM - 6:15 PM - Japanese conversation\n\n6:15 PM - 7:00 PM - English conversation\n\nEvent Description:\nThis is an in-person language exchange! Members are placed into groups of three or four based on their language level. Each 45 minute session consists of friendly casual conversation, and/or informal study.\n\nOptional Dinner :\nAfter the Language event, we usually go for Dinner. Dinner is optional, you may or may not join the Dinner, it depends on you.\nHowever, Dinner is only for Participants that joined on the day of the event.\n\nEvent Location:\nAtrium Food Court\n\nThe food court is directly connected to the Dundas subway station. Leave the subway station and walk west along Dundas Street.\n\nAt the intersection of Bay Street and Dundas Street, you will find an entrance. Proceed down the escalator.\n\nThe food court is on the basement floor. Please talk to the organizer with the signboard showing TJEX. (If you can’t find them, please send a message to the organizer.)\n\n⚠️RSVP & Late Policy:\nIf you are unable to join on the day of the event, please change your status from 'going-list' to 'not going-list'. Failure to Not show up will result in 1 No -Show. Also, in case of arriving 15 mins late to the event will result in 1 No-Show.\n\nMembers are removed from the group after 3 No-Shows.\n\nWaiting List:\nMembers can join the waiting-list even if an event is full. When a spot becomes available, we will move you to the going-list.\n\nGoing List:\nOnly Members on the going-list can participate on the day of the event.\n\nGroup Instagram -\n@tjex.ca\n\nFeel free to follow us!","startDate":"2026-10-03T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Atrium","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"595 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Japanese English Exchange (TJEX.ca)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tjex-ca/"},"performer":"Toronto Japanese English Exchange (TJEX.ca)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Brampton Dating for Character Matched Singles","url":"https://www.meetup.com/casual-moves-and-coffee-house-chess/events/316495674/","description":"**UPDATE: This gathering has been rescheduled and will commence at 5:00 PM on Sun, Oct 4 (local time).**\n\nVirtual speed dating via Zoom for individuals living in Brampton. Engage in brief individual sessions paired by age group, all from the comfort of your home.\n\nSimply confirm your attendance and we will contact you with the complete information. Availability is restricted and the event might be called off if participation is insufficient.","startDate":"2026-10-03T14:24:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"338 Kennedy Ave","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"338 Kennedy Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Casual Moves and Coffee House Chess","url":"https://www.meetup.com/casual-moves-and-coffee-house-chess/"},"performer":"Casual Moves and Coffee House Chess"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Japanese English Language Exchange — Manga Café","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tomodachitoronto/events/316726090/","description":"日本語のご案内は、英語のご案内の後に記載しています↓\nIf the event fills up, please join the waitlist! We may increase capacity. (waitlist is also used to verify members)\n満席の場合は、ぜひウェイトリストにご登録ください！定員を増やす場合があります (ウェイトリストは参加者確認も兼ねています)。\n\nThank you for your interest in our event! We are hosting a Japanese-English Language exchange at MottoMotto Cafe on Oct 3rd, from 12:00 PM to 2:30 PM. We'll have small groups of Japanese-English speakers, sorted by level, play some old-school J-pop, and sip on matcha.\n\n**$5 entry.**\nCash or E-Transfer tomodachitoronto@gmail.com\nThe cafe is hosting us, so grabbing a drink or an onigiri while you're there is really appreciated but not required.\n\n**Schedule**\n**11:50 AM:** Doors open\n**12:05 PM:** Round 1 of conversations (25 min English, 25 min Japanese)\n**12:55 PM:** Rotate partners\n**1:00 PM:** Round 2 of conversations (25 min English, 25 min Japanese)\n**1:50 PM:** Open social\n**2:30 PM:** Done\n\nご興味を持っていただきありがとうございます！\n\n日時：10月3日（土）12:00〜14:30\n会場：MottoMotto Cafe\n\n上記で日本語英語のLanguage Exchangeを開催します。\n\nレベル別の少人数グループに分かれて、懐かしい J-POP を聴きながら、抹茶を飲みつつ話しましょう。\n\n参加費：$5（現金または E-Transfer\n送金先：tomodachitoronto@gmail.com\n\nMottoMotto Cafeさんに会場をお借りしているので、ドリンクやおにぎりを注文していただけると本当に助かります（必須ではありません）。\n\nスケジュール\n11:50 開場\n12:05 ラウンド1（英語25分・日本語25分）\n12:55 グループチェンジ\n13:00 ラウンド2（英語25分・日本語25分）\n13:50 フリータイム。\n14:30 終了","startDate":"2026-10-03T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"MottoMotto Cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"300 Campbell Ave Unit 101, Toronto, ON M6P 3V6, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Tomodachi Toronto - Japanese x English Language Exchange","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tomodachitoronto/"},"performer":"Tomodachi Toronto - Japanese x English Language Exchange"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Saturday Harbourfront Autumn Leisure Social Walk! (Saturday, October 3rd)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316601866/","description":"Hello everyone,\n\n**\\*\\*Kindly Read Carefully\\*\\***\n\nPlease join me and my other groups for a great Saturday at the Harbour Front in Toronto. A great day to see the sites, meet lots of friendly people, grab a coffee, go for a leisure walk by the water, sip on a beverage/grab some dinner and enjoy the Toronto Downtown Night Life.\n(Both outdoor and indoor)\n\nI'm going to show you around, play a little ice breaker game or two; and then gravitate towards some places where we can relax and possibly even more than that. :)\n\n\\*The walking portion will be roughly 2.5 hours with rest periods/bathroom breaks, then we will find a casual place to chill and eat\n\nThis will be a fun day and night (Dress casual would be optimal for this event) (comfortable shoes would be best- for walking and chilling)\n\n\\*Arrive early if you like (however we will meet out front at\n3:00 p.m. (we will wait for everyone to arrive until roughly 3:30)\n\nWe will meet at **Starbucks, 208 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON M5J 2Y1** where you are welcome to grab a beverage or pastry if you like.\n\\*This will give us an opportunity to introduce ourselves as everyone arrives; then make our way on our small afternoon and early evening adventure through the Toronto Harbour Front and more.\n\nEvent details below:\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\n**Event Details:**\n**The Saturday Harbourfront Autumn Leisure Social Walk!**\n\n-A great day as we explore some of the best area's of the Harbour Front near the water, board walk and entertainment strip (lots of patio's, parks, festivals, bars, restaurants and cafes)\n-We can stop and rest at different spots, take some lovely scenic photos, group photos and share some laughs together\n-Perhaps play a couple ice breaker games near the beginning as well to help us get to know one another\n\n\\*A great way to naturally make connections, get some fresh air and enjoy our Saturday and Saturday Night together :)\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Event Fee:**\n10 dollars (cash only) when you arrive (HST is included)\nor e transfer in advance to Steveflemming11@gmail.com\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n**Time and Location: Where to meet us?**\n\nWe will meet at **Starbucks, 208 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON M5J 2Y1** where you are welcome to grab a beverage or pastry if you like.\n\n\\*Arrive early if you like (however we will meet out front at\n3:00 p.m. (we will wait for everyone to arrive until roughly 3:30)\n\nGo Train will take you Union Station- close walk from there:)\nPlenty of parking in that area too- but subway, and/or street car is highly recommended\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n***Thanks for reading everyone, remember to RSVP and see you real soon!*** :)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-","startDate":"2026-10-03T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Starbucks (Queens Quay) (Toronto)","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"208 Queens Quay W, ON M5J 2Y1, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🐾 Lend a Hand, Save Some Paws!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/events/316791840/","description":"Join us this Saturday for a small community volunteer effort to help spread the word about the M1L Trap-Neuter-Return (TNR) initiative.\n\nWe’ll meet near Santa Monica Blvd & St. Clair Ave E and distribute flyers in the surrounding neighbourhood. I’ll have the flyers with me and assign everyone an area to cover when we meet, so you don’t need to figure out the route beforehand.\n\n📬 The job is simple: walk around your assigned area and place the flyers in mailboxes. You can cover as much as you’re comfortable with.\n\n❤️ A couple of hours of our time can help reach many residents and support healthier lives for the neighbourhood’s stray and feral cats.\n\nCome join us, get some fresh air, meet a few fellow animal lovers, and do a little good! 🐾\n\nNo experience needed — just bring comfortable shoes and a willingness to help!","startDate":"2026-10-03T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Santa Monica Blvd","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"69 Clapperton Ave Scarborough, ON M1L 4K7, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe & Wander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/"},"performer":"Vibe & Wander"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"TOPHATs Nuit Blanche, a Blue Moon and a Beer Landing","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/events/316709104/","description":"Join Lawrence, your top hatted host, for an evening of Nuit Blanche art and Hops and Happy Hour treats.\n\nTemperature are to be around 10 C, so layer up as it will be cooler by the lake.\n\nWe will meet-up at Blue Moon Brewery at 7 pm for a refreshing Belgian brew.\n\nhttps://www.bluemooncanada.ca/en-CA/beers\n3 Tecumseth St\n\nAt 7:30 pmish, we will begin our Nuit Blanche adventure visiting the two exhibits in the STACKT Market\n\n“Magnetic Mother” by Micki-Lee Smith, Zakriya Bashir-Hill , Pratap Mathews #30\nRemember \\| Imagine by Hajar Moradi \\#29\n\nThen we will cross the Bathurst Street bridge, where you can get a scenic shot of our downtown as we head towards the lake.\n\nThe Bentway - Social Fabric: A Community Textile Activation by SHEEEP: Reza Nik, Sam Cruxton, Jocelyn Hernandez #64\n\nfollowed by The Bentway - A Persistent Crossing by Stanzie Tooth #65\n\nThen we will walk to Canoe Landing to see...\nKilim by Roda Medhat #53\nNight Waves by CityPlace and Fort York BIA\nFarsh by Roda Medhat #54\nGarrison Creek by Brian Leclerc #31\n\nAt 9 pmish is Happy Hour at Hunters Landing where we will rest, refresh before continuing on our adventure.\n\nhttps://www.thelandinggroup.ca/en/menu/hunters/happy-hour.html\n82 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON M5V 4A6\n\nBack down Bathurst to the lakeside to see\nOCAD University and the Delegation of the European Union to Canada - “The Light” and “Melting Temporalities” by Paul Murnaghan, Claire Brunet, Johnny Ranger #66\n\nThen over to one of my favourite summertime locations, the Toronto Music Garden to view.\nAscension by Ilene Sova #32\n\nWalking East along the waterfront we will arrive at The Grandmother Project by Peter Dillman #33\n\nSteps away is the Harbourfront Centre - Dance Stoops by Daily tous les jours #79\n\nOur final stop is at Love Park\nparol-parolan by HOT A!R ATEL!ER\n\nHere's the link to all the Nuit Blanche 2026 activities.\nhttps://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/festivals-events/nuitblanche/all-art-projects/","startDate":"2026-10-03T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/re